    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9610ebf3_98e5ba67",
        "filename": "health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 60,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-18T17:57:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No.\n\nIt is expected that RegisterEvent is called by subclass override of Init(), which should happen before MainLoop() starts. Note that RegisterEvent is a protected method.\n\nThat being said, healthd_register_event() exposes the function as a public API. Clients could incorrectly call it in a different thread after MainLoop() starts. Hence, this CHECK here is a sanity check to defend against this state.\n\nNote that reject_event_register_ is initialized to false and only set to true once in MainLoop(); it is never reset back to false. I think a bool here is necessary, and an atomic_bool is an overkill.\n\nLet me know if you think otherwise.",
      "parentUuid": "8813c8a9_86c24120",
      "revId": "50c9e25251cfabb53c44bf6486b6aa606d71852a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02a4dcef_6feec7dc",
        "filename": "health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 60,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120612
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-18T19:11:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah ok, SGTM. Will anything bad happen if a client incorrectly calls it in a different thread and it races with MainLoop() starting?",
      "parentUuid": "9610ebf3_98e5ba67",
      "revId": "50c9e25251cfabb53c44bf6486b6aa606d71852a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e71feca1_2f8d68f4",
        "filename": "health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 60,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-22T19:18:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. When these two functions are executed on a different thread, since this function writes the event_handlers_ vector and MainLoop() reads it, it can go segfault. \n\nOne way to fix this is to have a \"state\" variable in the class, and here, check that it is called during initialization only. I\u0027ll put up a CL.",
      "parentUuid": "02a4dcef_6feec7dc",
      "revId": "50c9e25251cfabb53c44bf6486b6aa606d71852a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e4132606_561cd241",
        "filename": "health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 60,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-22T19:22:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, MainLoop only reads the size() of event_handlers_. In a race, MainLoop may call epoll_wait() with a smaller event count, which may cause events to not be depleted. I think this is acceptable (and is an existing \"bug\" before my change, if it is a bug).\n\nWe only add event handlers at the end of event_handlers_, so it is fine.",
      "parentUuid": "e71feca1_2f8d68f4",
      "revId": "50c9e25251cfabb53c44bf6486b6aa606d71852a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
